# JL §5, `hA` at a proper power: the torsion by `1 + u + … + u^{l-1}`

`Work.ORBridgeTor.hA_of_torsion` (proved) deduces node N9's hypothesis `hA` from the injectivity of
right multiplication by the second component `β` of the presentation map — JL Lemma 5.1 + Claim 5.9
in the right-module form, i.e. node N8.  **That hypothesis fails when the relator is a proper power
`u ^ l` with `l ≥ 2`:** the Magnus presentation map has `β = (1 + u + … + u^{l-1}) · β₀`, and in
`K[G]` the factor `ν := 1 + u + … + u^{l-1}` is a zero divisor (`ν · (u - 1) = u^l - 1 = 0`), so
`(op β) • ·` is not injective.  This is obstruction (V3) of `OR_REMAINING_LEAD.md`.

What is true, and what the Magnus sequence actually needs, is the statement below: on the *quotient*
`A` of `K[G]` by the right ideal generated by `u - 1` — in the application
`A = K[G] / K[G](u - 1) = relationModule K r u` — the map
`(S ⊗[K] M) ⊗_{K[G]} A → (S ⊗[K] M) ⊗_{K[G]} B` induced by `f` is still injective.  The proof is
the one from `N8_TORSION_LEAD.md` (L7): from `x · ν · β₀ = 0` and the injectivity of `·β₀` derive
`x · ν = 0`; in characteristic zero this gives `x = x · (1 - l⁻¹ν)`, and
`1 - l⁻¹ν = (u - 1) · c` for the explicit `c` below (`(u-1) · Σ_{i<l} Σ_{j<i} u^j = ν - l`), so
`x = (op ((u-1)·c)) • x` and the balanced relation
`mk x ae = mk ((op r) • x) ae = mk x (r • ae) = mk x 0` kills `z`.

The statement needs no hypothesis beyond the two of `Work.ORBridgeTor.hA_of_torsion`: the
necessary `K`-linearity of the diagonal right action is obtained by moving the scalar to the
right (`l⁻¹ • ν = ν * (l⁻¹ • 1)`) before applying `MulOpposite.op_mul` and `mul_smul`, so that
`Work.ORFlatness.diagRightModule` is never unfolded.

## Main result

* `Work.ORFinal.hA_of_torsion_pow` — N9's `hA` from the *injectivity of `·β₀`* alone, at a
  presentation whose relator is a power `u ^ l` with `0 < l` and `char K = 0`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.ORBridgeTor.Defs
import Submission.Work.ORBridgeTor.HA
import Submission.Work.ORFinal.Antiaut

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000
set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

open TensorProduct MulOpposite

universe u

namespace Work.ORFinal

open Work.ORFlatness

/-- **N9's `hA` at a proper power `u ^ l`, in characteristic zero** (the replacement for
`Work.ORBridgeTor.hA_of_torsion` in the case `l ≥ 2`).

Let `S` be a `K`-algebra with `φ : K[G] →ₐ[K] S`, let `f : A →ₗ[K[G]] B` be a map of `K[G]`-modules
whose source `A` is generated by `ae` and **annihilated by the right ideal `K[G](u-1)`**
(`hae` — for `A = K[G]/K[G](u-1)` and `ae = 1` this is the quotient relation), and let the second
component of `f` on the generator be `ν · β₀` with `ν = Σ_{i<l} u^i`.  If right multiplication by
`β₀` is injective on the diagonal module `S ⊗[K] M` (node N8's Lemma 5.1′ in the right-module form),
then so is the map induced by `f` on the balanced tensor — node N9's `hA`.

The hypothesis `hae` is exactly "`ae` generates a quotient of `K[G]/K[G](u-1)`": it says that every
element of the right ideal generated by `u - 1` annihilates `ae`. -/
theorem hA_of_torsion_pow (K : Type u) [Field K] [CharZero K] (G : Type u) [Group G]
    (S : Type u) [Ring S] [Algebra K S] (φ : MonoidAlgebra K G →ₐ[K] S)
    (ug : MonoidAlgebra K G) (l : ℕ) (hl : 0 < l)
    (ν β₀ : MonoidAlgebra K G) (hν : ν = ∑ i ∈ Finset.range l, ug ^ i)
    {A : Type u} [AddCommGroup A] [Module (MonoidAlgebra K G) A]
    {B : Type u} [AddCommGroup B] [Module (MonoidAlgebra K G) B]
    (f : A →ₗ[MonoidAlgebra K G] B) (ae : A)
    (hgen : ∀ a : A, ∃ r : MonoidAlgebra K G, a = r • ae)
    (hae : ∀ c : MonoidAlgebra K G, ((ug - 1) * c) • ae = 0)
    (π : B →ₗ[MonoidAlgebra K G] (MonoidAlgebra K G))
    (hπf : π (f ae) = ν * β₀)
    (hβ₀ : ∀ (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module K M] [Module (MonoidAlgebra K G) M]
      [IsScalarTower K (MonoidAlgebra K G) M] [SMulCommClass K (MonoidAlgebra K G) M],
      letI := diagRightModule K G S φ M
      Function.Injective (fun x : S ⊗[K] M => (op β₀) • x)) :
    ∀ (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module K M] [Module (MonoidAlgebra K G) M]
      [IsScalarTower K (MonoidAlgebra K G) M] [SMulCommClass K (MonoidAlgebra K G) M],
      letI := diagRightModule K G S φ M
      Function.Injective (BalTensor.map (MonoidAlgebra K G)
        (LinearMap.id : (S ⊗[K] M) →ₗ[(MonoidAlgebra K G)ᵐᵒᵖ] (S ⊗[K] M)) f) := by
  intro M _ _ _ _ _
  letI := diagRightModule K G S φ M
  -- the explicit common factor `c` with `1 - l⁻¹ ν = (u - 1) * c`
  set S' : MonoidAlgebra K G := ∑ i ∈ Finset.range l, ∑ j ∈ Finset.range i, ug ^ j with hS'
  set c : MonoidAlgebra K G := -((l : K)⁻¹ • S') with hc
  have hl0 : (l : K) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr hl.ne'
  have hcast : (l : K)⁻¹ • (l : MonoidAlgebra K G) = 1 := by
    rw [Algebra.smul_def, ← map_natCast (algebraMap K (MonoidAlgebra K G)) l, ← map_mul,
      inv_mul_cancel₀ hl0, map_one]
  -- `(u - 1) * Σ_{i<l} Σ_{j<i} u^j = ν - l`
  have htel : ∀ i : ℕ, (ug - 1) * (∑ j ∈ Finset.range i, ug ^ j) = ug ^ i - 1 := by
    intro i
    rw [Finset.mul_sum]
    have hterm : ∀ j : ℕ, (ug - 1) * ug ^ j = ug ^ (j + 1) - ug ^ j := by
      intro j
      rw [sub_mul, one_mul, pow_succ']
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun j _ => hterm j)]
    rw [Finset.sum_range_sub (fun j => ug ^ j), pow_zero]
  have hsub : (ug - 1) * S' = ν - (l : MonoidAlgebra K G) := by
    rw [hS', Finset.mul_sum, hν,
      Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun i _ => htel i), Finset.sum_sub_distrib, Finset.sum_const,
      Finset.card_range, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  have hone : (ug - 1) * c = 1 - (l : K)⁻¹ • ν := by
    rw [hc, mul_neg, Algebra.mul_smul_comm, hsub, smul_sub, hcast, neg_sub]
  have key : ∀ z : BalTensor (MonoidAlgebra K G) (S ⊗[K] M) A,
      BalTensor.map (MonoidAlgebra K G)
        (LinearMap.id : (S ⊗[K] M) →ₗ[(MonoidAlgebra K G)ᵐᵒᵖ] (S ⊗[K] M)) f z = 0 → z = 0 := by
    intro z hz
    have hmem : ∀ (x : S ⊗[K] M) (a : A),
        BalTensor.mk (MonoidAlgebra K G) x a ∈
          (BalTensor.mkLeft (MonoidAlgebra K G) ae).range := by
      intro x a
      obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := hgen a
      refine ⟨op r • x, ?_⟩
      show BalTensor.mk (MonoidAlgebra K G) (op r • x) ae
        = BalTensor.mk (MonoidAlgebra K G) x (r • ae)
      rw [BalTensor.mk_smul_right]
    have hzrange : z ∈ (BalTensor.mkLeft (MonoidAlgebra K G) ae).range :=
      (AddSubgroup.closure_le _).mpr (by
        rintro y ⟨⟨x, a⟩, rfl⟩
        exact hmem x a)
        (BalTensor.mem_closure_mk (R := MonoidAlgebra K G) z)
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hzrange
    have hx' : BalTensor.mk (MonoidAlgebra K G) x ae = z := hx
    have h1 : BalTensor.mk (MonoidAlgebra K G) x (f ae) = 0 := by
      rw [← hx'] at hz
      rw [BalTensor.map_mk] at hz
      simpa using hz
    have h2 : BalTensor.mk (MonoidAlgebra K G) x (ν * β₀) = 0 := by
      have h3 : BalTensor.map (MonoidAlgebra K G)
          (LinearMap.id : (S ⊗[K] M) →ₗ[(MonoidAlgebra K G)ᵐᵒᵖ] (S ⊗[K] M)) π
          (BalTensor.mk (MonoidAlgebra K G) x (f ae)) = 0 := by
        rw [h1, map_zero]
      rw [BalTensor.map_mk, LinearMap.id_coe, id_eq, hπf] at h3
      exact h3
    have h4 : (op (ν * β₀)) • x = 0 :=
      (Work.ORBridgeTor.balTensor_mk_eq_zero_iff (MonoidAlgebra K G) (S ⊗[K] M) x (ν * β₀)).mp h2
    have h5 : (op ν) • x = 0 := by
      have h6 : (op β₀) • ((op ν) • x) = 0 := by
        rw [← mul_smul, ← MulOpposite.op_mul, h4]
      exact hβ₀ M (by
        show (op β₀) • ((op ν) • x) = (op β₀) • (0 : S ⊗[K] M)
        rw [h6, smul_zero])
    have h7 : x = (op (1 - (l : K)⁻¹ • ν)) • x := by
      have h9 : (1 : MonoidAlgebra K G) - (l : K)⁻¹ • ν
          = 1 - ν * ((l : K)⁻¹ • (1 : MonoidAlgebra K G)) := by
        rw [Algebra.smul_def (l : K)⁻¹ ν, Algebra.smul_def (l : K)⁻¹ (1 : MonoidAlgebra K G),
          mul_one, Algebra.commutes]
      rw [h9, MulOpposite.op_sub, MulOpposite.op_mul, sub_smul, mul_smul, h5, smul_zero,
        MulOpposite.op_one, one_smul, sub_zero]
    have h8 : x = (op ((ug - 1) * c)) • x := by
      rw [← hone] at h7
      exact h7
    rw [← hx', h8, BalTensor.mk_smul_right, hae c, BalTensor.mk_zero_right]
  intro z z' hzz
  have h2 : BalTensor.map (MonoidAlgebra K G)
      (LinearMap.id : (S ⊗[K] M) →ₗ[(MonoidAlgebra K G)ᵐᵒᵖ] (S ⊗[K] M)) f (z - z') = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, hzz, sub_self]
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (key (z - z') h2)

end Work.ORFinal
